    "description": "Develop and maintain applications within a large-scale COBOL-based mainframe system with an attached web app, serving as the backbone of core financial operations for one of the largest brokerage platforms in existence.\n\nWork within a platform comprising 10M+ lines of code, thousands of batch jobs, hundreds of CICS programs, and decades of accumulated legacy complexity, interfacing with dozens of internal systems and connecting to multiple external vendors via both real-time MQ and batch NDM.\n\nDesign and implement capabilities supporting mission-critical industry initiatives, regulatory changes, and strategic business enhancements.\n\nAnalyze and enhance complex legacy code to improve system stability and maintainability while ensuring architectural consistency across interdependent batch and online components.\n\nLead root cause analysis and resolution of high-severity production incidents.\nSupport and troubleshoot batch job streams, coordinating with scheduling systems to maintain SLA adherence.\nCollaborate with business stakeholders to translate requirements into scalable technical solutions.\nProvide technical guidance and code review oversight across the team, establishing standards for development and ensuring new code is stable and maintainable.\nOwn projects end-to-end, frequently serving as the sole technical contributor and primary point of contact for international asset clearing initiatives.",
